<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	R13: under the hardened runtime, TCC refuses to even ASK for the calendar
	unless the process holds this entitlement. The usage strings in
	Info.plist are not enough on their own, and the refusal is silent:
	requestFullAccessToEvents() returns false in about 25 ms without
	throwing, the authorization status stays notDetermined, and no prompt is
	ever shown. tccd says so in as many words (macOS 26.6.2, guest log,
	2026-09-21):

	    Prompting policy for hardened runtime; service: kTCCServiceCalendar
	    requires entitlement com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars
	    but it is missing for accessing={... dev.facens.meetinghop ...}
	    Policy disallows prompt for Sub:{dev.facens.meetinghop}; access to
	    kTCCServiceCalendar denied

	With it, the same build prompts "Allow Full Access" and the grant sticks.
	This app is not sandboxed; the entitlement is a hardened-runtime resource
	grant, and it is the only one MeetingHop carries — it sends no Apple
	Events.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
